                <Description>
                    <p>UtmcXml is an XML representation of the Urban Traffic Management Control model that can be used to exchange data objects between UTMC databases and other services.</p>. 
                    <p>This subschema describes the UTMC Transport Link Data Object. A Transport Link describes a route  through the transport network from an origin to a destination, possibly via a specified point. It may be composed of an ordered list of <b>Route Segments </b> and  may include:
                    <ol>
                            <li>Definition, describing the fixed properties of an object and its location on the network</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link Definition</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Configuration  Objects, describing configurable properties of objects, with a time of last change</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link ANPR Configuration, describing a transport link monitored by an ANPR camera </li>
                                <li>Transport Link GPS  Configuration, describing a transport link monitored by GPS probes</li>
                                <li>Transport Link Scoot Configuration, describing a transport link monitored by a  Scoot system.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Dynamic  Objects, describing volatile properties of Data Objects, with a time of last change</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link ANPR Dynamic, describing a transport link flow values from   an ANPR system.</li>
                                <li>Transport Link GPS Dynamic, describing a transport link flow values from  GPS probes.</li>
                                <li>Transport Link Scoot Dynamic, describing a transport link flow values from   a  Scoot system.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Device History, describing the device history which may be issued to the device.</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link Device History</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Fault, describing the device  faults,</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link Fault</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Command, describing the commands which may be issued to the device.</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link Command</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Types, describing the allowed values for types associated with a Transport Link.</li>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Transport Link Type Definition</li>
                                <li>Transport Link State Type Definition</li>
                                <li>Transport Link Quality Type Definition</li>
                                <li>Transport Link Fault  Type Definition</li>
                            </ul>
                        </ol>
                    </p>
                </Description>
